<title>MALAYSIA: Malaysia Feb 1-20 palm oil exports 269,684t-SGS.</title>
<headline>Malaysia Feb 1-20 palm oil exports 269,684t-SGS.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cargo surveyor Societe Generale de Surveillance (SGS) Malaysia Sdn Bhd said it estimated Malaysia's palm oil exports for February 1-20 at 269,684 tonnes against 302,702 in January 1-20.</p>
<p>It said the exports comprised 92,007 tonnes of RBD palm oil, 104,273 tonnes of RBD palm olein and 29,400 tonnes of RBD palm stearin. The other products were 44,004 tonnes.  </p>
<p>Pakistan was the main buyer during the period, taking 53,132 tonnes, followed by Japan 29,540 tonnes, India 23,920 tonnes and China 23,118.</p>
<p>Countries in the European Union bought 43,414 tonnes.</p>
<p>-- Kuala Lumpur newsroom (603-230-7510)</p>
